    "matches_claimed_nav_left": true,
    "honesty": "applied_vx is the clamped command, not odometry. Forward clamp is 0.056 m/s, lowered from 0.080 because 0.080 yaws off and tips near 1.2 m (support margin about \u22120.09 m). CPG amplitude is |applied_vx| / 0.080, so full forward stick is amplitude 0.70 and reverse -0.032 m/s stays amplitude 0.40 with stance damper 100 N/(m/s). Yaw cap is \u00b10.25 rad/s; hip-yaw clip 0.12 rad plus outside-step scale 0.20. Right-turn swing hip yaw keeps 0.60 of that clip so the foot does not land toed against the turn; stance hip yaw and the cold-start left turn are unchanged. After the gait has been walking for 12 s, a left yaw command drops the 0.06 rad bias and uses outside-step scale 0.24. Measured motion \u0394x=+0.598 m, mean body vx=+0.038 m/s (not the command). Straight-forward net yaw drift=-0.68 deg; yaw during that window -15.1 to +3.7 deg. Heading at the end of the clip is +72.01 deg from the start. Turn-window \u0394yaw=+75.75 deg (mean yaw rate +0.106 rad/s, cap \u00b10.25). tip=False; CoP in box=True (outside 0.0000 m); peak leg torque=2.10 Nm (limit 2.1). Stance-slip damper is 25 N/(m/s) while walking forward, down from the CSF50 crawl's 115. After stop it is 100 N/(m/s) for 1.20 s (pose blend 0.70 s), then off. A reverse stop finishes at most one step first if that phase would pitch. Foot box, friction, kp, and \u00b12.1 Nm are unchanged. Nav: approach \u0394x=+0.598 m (mean body vx +0.038 m/s), turn \u0394yaw=+75.7 deg (mean yaw rate +0.106 rad/s, mean body vx +0.044 m/s), resume along heading +0.317 m (mean body vx +0.051 m/s)."
  },
